  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Multi-Head Attention (MHA)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport math\n\ndef inference_multi_head_attention(Q: list, K: list, V: list, num_heads: int) -> list:\n    q = np.array(Q, dtype=float)\n    k = np.array(K, dtype=float)\n    v = np.array(V, dtype=float)\n    B, S, D = q.shape\n    H = int(num_heads)\n    dk = D // H\n    qh = q.reshape(B, S, H, dk).swapaxes(1, 2)\n    kh = k.reshape(B, S, H, dk).swapaxes(1, 2)\n    vh = v.reshape(B, S, H, dk).swapaxes(1, 2)\n    scores = (qh @ kh.swapaxes(-1, -2)) / math.sqrt(dk)\n    exps = np.exp(scores - np.max(scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    attn = exps / np.sum(exps, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    out = (attn @ vh).swapaxes(1, 2).reshape(B, S, D)\n    return np.round(out, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
